WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.175 --> 00:00:01.667
- Jazz and I are looking at the email

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.434
of the things we can't eat.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.506
Can't eat eggs.

00:00:04.506 --> 00:00:05.655
- Oh, fuck.

00:00:05.655 --> 00:00:08.238
(bright music)

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.516
- I really like any type of food

00:00:11.516 --> 00:00:15.026
except for like really,
really vegetable-heavy foods.

00:00:15.026 --> 00:00:16.867
- I'm not used to looking at labels.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:19.600
I wanna get a lot of knowledge
into what goes into foods

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.245
and I think hopefully my
diet's better after this,

00:00:22.245 --> 00:00:24.054
and hopefully I learn
how to cook something.

00:00:24.054 --> 00:00:26.313
- I just went on this journey of having

00:00:26.313 --> 00:00:30.480
healthy relationships with
myself, food and exercise,

00:00:31.866 --> 00:00:35.305
and I'm just excited to
start something new and do it

00:00:35.305 --> 00:00:38.524
in a healthy, positive mental space.

00:00:38.524 --> 00:00:41.290
- We're going on our
first grocery mission.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.130
I don't know what to look for.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.776
Maybe we'll just go to
what we normally get

00:00:44.776 --> 00:00:46.632
and then look for options.

00:00:46.632 --> 00:00:49.646
We've made it to the fruit section

00:00:49.646 --> 00:00:52.374
which we can guarantee is vegan.

00:00:52.374 --> 00:00:53.777
- I found some meatless meats.

00:00:53.777 --> 00:00:55.793
I'm here for sausage!

00:00:55.793 --> 00:00:58.705
Not in my sexual life, just in this life.

00:00:58.705 --> 00:01:00.147
- [Lindsay] We're going
for the safe options.

00:01:00.147 --> 00:01:00.980
- Safe option.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:02.806
Probably not that healthy
but spaghetti's good.

00:01:02.806 --> 00:01:04.350
- I feel like I'm trying
things that I've always

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.012
wanted to try but now trying
stuff I have a reason to.

00:01:07.012 --> 00:01:07.943
- I'm actually excited.

00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:09.346
I got a lot (chuckles).

00:01:09.346 --> 00:01:10.874
I don't know if I can
even eat all of these.

00:01:10.874 --> 00:01:12.430
I probably will because
I'm gonna be hungry.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:15.052
- Alright, let's try this vegan sausage.

00:01:15.052 --> 00:01:19.280
I put some mustard on
it - that's vegan too.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.519
Consistency, a little
questionable, but taste?

00:01:22.519 --> 00:01:23.352
Very good!

00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:25.932
Oh my god, that actually
kinda tastes like sausage.

00:01:25.932 --> 00:01:28.446
- [Jazzmyne] We have
a little meeting today

00:01:28.446 --> 00:01:32.037
and here's all the food that I can't eat.

00:01:32.037 --> 00:01:33.621
- Alright so we had catered lunch today

00:01:33.621 --> 00:01:35.218
and there was tons of sandwiches

00:01:35.218 --> 00:01:38.310
all of which had meat except one,

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.143
and it has tofu.

00:01:39.143 --> 00:01:42.236
I do not like tofu but I
am sticking it out today.

00:01:42.236 --> 00:01:43.069
- Oh!

00:01:49.386 --> 00:01:51.999
- Me and my friend were
talking and she's vegan.

00:01:51.999 --> 00:01:55.406
She was saying how she gets
annoyed when people do this shit

00:01:55.406 --> 00:01:58.542
because he will starve and
just don't end up eating

00:01:58.542 --> 00:02:00.051
because they can't eat anything.

00:02:00.051 --> 00:02:02.251
And so I've really been
making it a priority

00:02:02.251 --> 00:02:05.037
to make sure I'm not starving and I'm not.

00:02:05.037 --> 00:02:07.522
I feel very full and I'm eating vegetables

00:02:07.522 --> 00:02:10.689
and I'm eating fruits and I feel good.

00:02:14.141 --> 00:02:16.558
(she laughs)

00:02:20.554 --> 00:02:24.584
- So today I realized that
not all vegan food is healthy.

00:02:24.584 --> 00:02:26.222
I know that's kind of dumb to realize.

00:02:26.222 --> 00:02:27.650
I snacked a lot.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:28.874
I had Oreos.

00:02:28.874 --> 00:02:30.306
I had chips.

00:02:30.306 --> 00:02:33.372
There was a lot of things
you can eat when you're vegan

00:02:33.372 --> 00:02:35.601
and not all of them are great for you

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.378
so I think from now on I
kinda need to watch myself,

00:02:38.378 --> 00:02:40.624
make sure I'm just
getting nutrients I need.

00:02:40.624 --> 00:02:43.208
- So it's about 2:30 AM.

00:02:43.208 --> 00:02:47.583
Usually right now, I would make
an egg sandwich with cheese

00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:51.230
but I can't because I can't have eggs.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:55.397
So my lunch today is sausageless
sausage and broccoli.

00:02:59.032 --> 00:03:02.300
- I'm at the mall and I keep smelling

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.868
Wetzel's freaking Pretzels
and I can't eat it

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:07.069
and it's killing me.

00:03:07.069 --> 00:03:11.161
- We are on our way to go
to an all-vegan restaurant!

00:03:11.161 --> 00:03:12.008
- [Girls] Whoo!

00:03:12.008 --> 00:03:12.884
- We're here.

00:03:12.884 --> 00:03:13.717
We're looking at the menus.

00:03:13.717 --> 00:03:15.452
The best part of this is that we can

00:03:15.452 --> 00:03:16.897
just choose whatever's on this menu.

00:03:16.897 --> 00:03:17.730
- All vegan.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.730
- All vegan.

00:03:35.775 --> 00:03:38.608
- So after being vegan for a week,

00:03:39.907 --> 00:03:44.410
I've realized that it's
truly fucking amazing.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.092
The meatless meat options,
it still made me feel

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:49.885
like I was eating meat but
I felt better about it,

00:03:49.885 --> 00:03:53.519
honestly because I knew
I wasn't eating animals.

00:03:53.519 --> 00:03:55.405
- I think it really just
opened my eyes to the fact that

00:03:55.405 --> 00:03:58.262
I just need to start reading
my labels of the things I eat

00:03:58.262 --> 00:04:02.268
because honestly, the things
that even are good to eat,

00:04:02.268 --> 00:04:03.370
that don't have vegan
stuff in it, I'm like,

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:06.135
oh my God, they have this
amount of sugar and other things

00:04:06.135 --> 00:04:08.014
that I should be looking
at and paying attention to.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.400
- I'm really glad I did this challenge

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.347
and from now on I can
definitely see myself

00:04:11.347 --> 00:04:13.588
exploring a lot more options on food.

00:04:13.588 --> 00:04:17.588
- So yes, I will be
continuing some vegan habits

00:04:19.042 --> 00:04:21.106
but also yes, I am
driving to Korean barbecue

00:04:21.106 --> 00:04:22.284
at this very moment.

00:04:22.284 --> 00:04:25.767
(crowd chatter)

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:27.055
- I just ate an egg.

00:04:27.055 --> 00:04:28.727
I just ate a fucking egg!

00:04:28.727 --> 00:04:31.144
(soft music)

